# Shell scripts and the Gradle wrapper are executed by bash/sh (WSL, Linux CI, the GPL "rebuild from
# source" recipe in licenses/FFMPEG_SOURCE.txt). A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would turn
# them into CRLF, and bash then fails on the first line ("set -euo pipefail\r: invalid option name"),
# so they are LF in every working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
# ...and the Windows batch wrapper stays CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Committed binaries (the arm64 libffmpeg.so and the impersonation bundle): never line-ending-converted.
*.so binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
